    <briefdescription>
<para>Non-owning view of a non-commutative word: <computeroutput>[<ref refid="class_word_a20e33cf76cae20a1b09c6419d6f71ad2_1a20e33cf76cae20a1b09c6419d6f71ad2" kindref="member">begin</ref>, <ref refid="class_word_a57a3bd2eb17ecc840adc2236a9cfb157_1a57a3bd2eb17ecc840adc2236a9cfb157" kindref="member">end</ref>)</computeroutput> of <computeroutput><ref refid="classint" kindref="compound">int</ref></computeroutput> variable indices. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Stores three pointers / lengths (<computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_a6b3128c4ff711018aa7c260c32f15e0b_1a6b3128c4ff711018aa7c260c32f15e0b" kindref="member">mBegin</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_a5428e2e40693dbb68b45d20ce164bc90_1a5428e2e40693dbb68b45d20ce164bc90" kindref="member">mEnd</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_a41988b1f6413e08d2d9d986016f80188_1a41988b1f6413e08d2d9d986016f80188" kindref="member">mSize</ref></computeroutput>) into an externally owned buffer (typically a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_memory_block" kindref="compound">MemoryBlock</ref></computeroutput> arena in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_n_c_f4" kindref="compound">NCF4</ref></computeroutput>). The view is cheap to copy and pass around but the caller must keep the backing buffer alive for the <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput>&apos;s lifetime. Equality is elementwise; iteration goes through <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_a20e33cf76cae20a1b09c6419d6f71ad2_1a20e33cf76cae20a1b09c6419d6f71ad2" kindref="member">begin()</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_a57a3bd2eb17ecc840adc2236a9cfb157_1a57a3bd2eb17ecc840adc2236a9cfb157" kindref="member">end()</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput>operator[]</computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
